1
00:00:00,602 --> 00:00:03,672
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,705 --> 00:00:06,340
♪ SOMEWHERE IN TIME
AND SPACE ♪

3
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:09,577
♪ MIKE NELSON
AND HIS ROBOT PALS ♪

4
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:12,647
♪ ARE CAUGHT IN
AN ENDLESS CHASE ♪

5
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:15,683
♪ PURSUED BY A WOMAN
WHOSE NAME IS PEARL ♪

6
00:00:15,717 --> 00:00:18,887
♪ AN EVIL GAL WHO WANTS
TO RULE THE WORLD ♪

7
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:21,790
♪ SHE THREW A FEW THINGS
IN HER PURSE ♪

8
00:00:21,823 --> 00:00:23,658
♪ AND IN HER ROCKET SHIP
SHE HUNTS HIM ♪

9
00:00:23,692 --> 00:00:25,660
♪ ALL ACROSS THE UNIVERSE ♪

10
00:00:25,693 --> 00:00:28,262
[PEARL]
I'LL GET YOU!

11
00:00:28,295 --> 00:00:31,132
♪ I'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

12
00:00:31,165 --> 00:00:34,702
♪ THE WORST I CAN FIND--
LA LA LA ♪

13
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:37,772
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:37,805 --> 00:00:40,708
♪ AND I'LL MONITOR HIS MIND--
LA LA LA ♪

15
00:00:40,742 --> 00:00:43,778
♪ NOW, KEEP IN MIND,
MIKE CAN'T CONTROL ♪

16
00:00:43,812 --> 00:00:47,082
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES BEGIN
OR END-- LA LA LA ♪

17
00:00:47,115 --> 00:00:50,152
♪ HE'LL TRY TO KEEP
HIS SANITY ♪

18
00:00:50,185 --> 00:00:52,720
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

19
00:00:55,157 --> 00:00:56,690
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL ♪

20
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,192
YOU'RE ON!

21
00:00:58,225 --> 00:00:59,393
OH, MY STARS!

22
00:00:59,427 --> 00:01:01,062
CHECK ME OUT!

23
00:01:01,095 --> 00:01:02,663
I'M DIFFERENT!

24
00:01:02,697 --> 00:01:03,965
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW ♪

25
00:01:03,998 --> 00:01:05,800
♪ HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

26
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:08,970
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS--
LA LA LA ♪

27
00:01:09,003 --> 00:01:12,407
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

28
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:15,310
♪ I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX" ♪

29
00:01:15,343 --> 00:01:18,045
♪ FOR MYSTERY
SCIENCE THEATER ♪

30
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:21,783
♪ 3000 ♪

31
00:01:34,328 --> 00:01:36,898
HI, EVERYONE. WELCOME
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

32
00:01:36,898 --> 00:01:38,867
MY NAME IS MIKE NELSON.

33
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,435
OR IT USED TO BE.

34
00:01:40,468 --> 00:01:43,103
YOU SEE, UNTIL RECENTLY,
I WAS JUST LIKE YOU.

35
00:01:43,137 --> 00:01:45,440
I BELIEVED THAT EVERYTHING THAT
WAS TAUGHT ME WAS RIGHT,

36
00:01:45,473 --> 00:01:47,742
AND EVERYTHING
WAS AS IT SEEMED.

37
00:01:47,775 --> 00:01:49,443
AND THEN ONE DAY,
I FOUND MYSELF PURSUED

38
00:01:49,477 --> 00:01:51,512
BY AGENTS OF
A SECRET GOVERNMENT PROJECT

39
00:01:51,545 --> 00:01:54,348
WHO BASICALLY WIPED OUT
EVERY SHRED OF EVIDENCE

40
00:01:54,382 --> 00:01:56,150
THAT I EVER EXISTED.

41
00:01:56,183 --> 00:01:57,718
THEY TOOK EVERYTHING,

42
00:01:57,752 --> 00:02:00,655
MY IDENTITY, MY LIFE.

43
00:02:00,688 --> 00:02:01,788
NOW I'M ON THE RUN,

44
00:02:01,823 --> 00:02:03,257
NEVER KNOWING
WHEN I'LL BE CAUGHT,

45
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:05,760
OR WHERE MY ENEMIES
WILL TURN UP.

46
00:02:05,793 --> 00:02:07,362
BUT THEY SHOULD KNOW,

47
00:02:07,395 --> 00:02:10,532
I WILL DO ANYTHING
TO GET BACK WHAT IS MINE.

48
00:02:10,565 --> 00:02:11,867
- HEY, MIKE!
- HEY, MIKE!

49
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,233
- MIKE.
- YEAH?

50
00:02:13,267 --> 00:02:14,568
WE FOUND YOUR WALLET.
IT WAS IN YOUR ROOM.

51
00:02:14,602 --> 00:02:15,937
- OH. [LAUGHS]
- YEAH.

52
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:17,805
EVERYTHING ABOUT YOUR IDENTITY
IS THERE, YOU CAN RELAX.

53
00:02:17,838 --> 00:02:19,207
GUESS I DIDN'T HAVE TO
DO VERY MUCH AT ALL

54
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,575
TO GET BACK WHAT'S MINE.

55
00:02:20,608 --> 00:02:22,077
- NO.
- YOU WEREN'T TELLING THEM ABOUT

56
00:02:22,110 --> 00:02:23,912
THE SECRET GOVERNMENT
CONSPIRACY, WERE YOU?

57
00:02:23,945 --> 00:02:25,247
WELL, MY WALLET WAS MISSING.

58
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,815
NOW, FOLKS, LISTEN,
PAY NO ATTENTION TO THIS GUY.

59
00:02:27,848 --> 00:02:30,150
EVERYTHING IS
EXACTLY AS IT SEEMS.

60
00:02:30,185 --> 00:02:32,187
AH, WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK--
WAIT A MINUTE...

61
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:34,488
WAIT A MINUTE, HOW DO I KNOW
THIS WALLET IS MINE?

62
00:02:34,522 --> 00:02:36,858
IT IS. LOOK, SAME PICTURE
OF MARK SPITZ, EVEN.

63
00:02:36,892 --> 00:02:40,093
- OH, GOOD.
- SAD, REALLY.

64
00:02:40,127 --> 00:02:42,097
♪♪

65
00:02:47,735 --> 00:02:49,870
GOTTA SAY, IT'S GOOD
TO HAVE THE OLD IDENTITY BACK--

66
00:02:49,903 --> 00:02:51,505
- AAH! AAH!
- WHAT? WHAT?

67
00:02:51,538 --> 00:02:52,873
THEY TOOK--
THE TOOK MY IDENTITY!

68
00:02:52,907 --> 00:02:55,277
EVERYTHING I EVER-- OH, WAIT,
IT'S RIGHT HERE. SORRY.

69
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:57,012
PHEW.
OH, MRS. FORRESTER'S CALLING.

70
00:02:57,045 --> 00:02:59,947
AND YOU WANT TO HANG ON
TO AN IDENTITY LIKE THAT, HUH?

71
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,582
SHEESH.

72
00:03:01,615 --> 00:03:04,052
- ALOHA! WELCOME ABOARD.
- ALOHA!

73
00:03:04,085 --> 00:03:07,122
WELCOME. BOBO,
I THINK THE IDEA

74
00:03:07,155 --> 00:03:08,890
IS TO DISTRIBUTE THEM
ONE-BY-ONE,

75
00:03:08,923 --> 00:03:11,225
AND THEN LET THE GUESTS
HANDLE IT FROM THERE.

76
00:03:11,258 --> 00:03:13,193
OH, I GET IT. SILLY ME.

77
00:03:13,227 --> 00:03:14,262
HELLO! ALOHA! WELCOME!

78
00:03:14,295 --> 00:03:16,197
BOBO, YOU IDIOT!

79
00:03:16,230 --> 00:03:18,498
COME, LET ME SHOW YOU
TO A CABIN.

80
00:03:18,532 --> 00:03:20,968
- OW! OW!
- ARRIVEDERCI!

81
00:03:21,002 --> 00:03:22,637
SON OF NEL, LISTEN.

82
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:24,505
OUR PHONE NUMBER
ACCIDENTALLY GOT PRINTED

83
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:26,473
IN AN AD
FOR A CRUISE SHIP DEAL.

84
00:03:26,507 --> 00:03:30,678
BOBO TOOK 2,500 RESERVATIONS
BEFORE HE TOLD ME.

85
00:03:30,712 --> 00:03:34,248
BUT THE MONEY'S SO SWEET,
I DECIDED TO KEEP IT.

86
00:03:34,282 --> 00:03:37,085
THEN WE LEFT PORT
BEFORE THEY COULD GET ON.

87
00:03:37,118 --> 00:03:38,920
[CHUCKLING]

88
00:03:38,953 --> 00:03:40,988
WELL, EXCEPT
FOR THOSE TWO EARLY NERDS.

89
00:03:41,022 --> 00:03:43,090
BUT...
[CHUCKLING]

90
00:03:43,123 --> 00:03:50,197
WE LEFT 2,498 SUCKERS ASHORE.
[CHUCKLING]

91
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,233
[CHUCKLING]

92
00:03:52,267 --> 00:03:56,972
BUT YOU LIVE IN A CASTLE, SO...
[CHUCKLING]

93
00:03:57,005 --> 00:04:00,207
SHUT UP. OKAY, WE GOTTA GIVE 'EM
THE WHOLE Q.E.-II DEAL,

94
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,010
SO WE NEED ICE SCULPTURES
FOR THE BUFFET TABLE.

95
00:04:03,043 --> 00:04:05,647
HEY, HEY, CLOROX FACE,
SEND THEM THE RAW MATERIALS.

96
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,015
AYE AYE, SIR!

97
00:04:07,082 --> 00:04:09,683
SHUT UP AND JUST DO IT.

98
00:04:09,717 --> 00:04:12,087
RIGHT.
[DIGITAL SOUND]

99
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,055
BOY...

100
00:04:14,088 --> 00:04:17,158
- HUH?
- HUH.

101
00:04:17,192 --> 00:04:18,993
HUH.

102
00:04:19,027 --> 00:04:21,295
ANNE AND I WOULD LIKE
TO SEE THE UPPER DECK NOW.

103
00:04:21,328 --> 00:04:24,465
OH, SURE, BUT-- OH, THE SEAS
ARE TOO ROUGH RIGHT NOW!

104
00:04:24,498 --> 00:04:27,102
- OH, YES.
- WHOA, FEEL THAT?

105
00:04:27,135 --> 00:04:29,070
TOO ROUGH TO FEED YOU, EVEN.

106
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:32,773
BUT STILL,
SMELL THAT SALT AIR.

107
00:04:32,807 --> 00:04:35,142
I'M GETTING SICK, NORM.

108
00:04:35,175 --> 00:04:37,112
MRS. DASH AIR, ACTUALLY.

109
00:04:37,145 --> 00:04:39,780
HEY MAW GIVER, IT'S NOT
TOO ROUGH TO FEED ME, IS IT?

110
00:04:39,813 --> 00:04:41,548
I MEAN, IT'S NOT TOO ROUGH--
OH!

111
00:04:41,582 --> 00:04:43,550
OKAY, LET'S SEE WHAT YOU GOT.

112
00:04:43,583 --> 00:04:45,787
WELL, NOW, I MADE A,
SORT OF, ENVIRONMENTAL SCULPTURE

113
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:47,055
WITH MY ICE.

114
00:04:47,088 --> 00:04:49,657
SETTING IT IN A SURROUNDING
OF GIN AND TONIC.

115
00:04:49,690 --> 00:04:52,793
AESTHETICALLY PLEASING,
AND VERY, VERY REFRESHING.

116
00:04:52,827 --> 00:04:55,630
UH, I UH...

117
00:04:55,663 --> 00:04:57,765
I-- I TRIED TO...

118
00:04:57,798 --> 00:04:59,067
TO WELD MINE.

119
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:02,570
- AND, UH...
- YEAH, YOU DID.

120
00:05:02,603 --> 00:05:04,138
I DON'T KNOW.

121
00:05:04,172 --> 00:05:08,175
WELL, I GIVE YOU
MICHELANGELO'S DAVID.

122
00:05:08,208 --> 00:05:10,043
WOW, CROW, BIGGER
THAN THE ORIGINAL.

123
00:05:10,077 --> 00:05:12,680
- AND OUT OF FOUR ICE CUBES?
- I'M JUST EFFICIENT, I GUESS.

124
00:05:12,747 --> 00:05:15,315
- MAN.
- YEAH, I COULD HAVE, UH...

125
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:18,152
COULD HAVE DONE THAT, I GUESS,
BUT I-- I WAS, UH...

126
00:05:18,185 --> 00:05:19,320
TRYING TO WELD MINE, AND--

127
00:05:19,353 --> 00:05:22,690
RIGHT, MIKE,
YOU MADE THAT CLEAR.

128
00:05:22,723 --> 00:05:25,125
AND NOW IT'S TIME
FOR YOUR ON-DECK MOVIE.

129
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:26,493
TO BE HELD BELOW DECKS TODAY

130
00:05:26,527 --> 00:05:29,297
BECAUSE OF
THE AFOREMENTIONED ROUGH SEAS.

131
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:31,265
[SHOUTING]

132
00:05:31,298 --> 00:05:32,633
IT'S CALLED DEVIL FISH,

133
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:34,468
AND IT FEATURES
MANY NAUTICAL THEMES

134
00:05:34,535 --> 00:05:37,205
AND MANY ITALIANS
PRETENDING TO BE FLORIDIANS.

135
00:05:37,238 --> 00:05:39,107
MIKE AND BOTS, ALSO ENJOY.

136
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:40,508
- BRAIN PAN, SEND IT.
- YEAH.

137
00:05:40,542 --> 00:05:42,477
[DIGITAL SOUND]

138
00:05:44,878 --> 00:05:47,382
HE JUST NEEDS
A LITTLE OFF THE CALF HERE.

139
00:05:47,415 --> 00:05:48,750
NO, STOP IT!

140
00:05:48,783 --> 00:05:50,385
GOOD GRAVY, MAN.
DON'T YOU EVER LEARN?

141
00:05:50,418 --> 00:05:51,352
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

142
00:05:51,385 --> 00:05:53,587
SORRY-- OH, WE GOT
MOVIE SIGN!

143
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:55,557
NO ACCUMULATED KNOWLEDGE
AT ALL.

144
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:08,168
[MIKE]
SORRY.

145
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:09,870
[CROW]
IT'S OKAY.

146
00:06:09,903 --> 00:06:15,410
HEY, BEBE REBOZO'S
HOME MOVIES.

147
00:06:15,443 --> 00:06:16,777
I TOLD HIM, YOU KNOW.

148
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:18,813
AND I TOLD HER,
LOUDLY AND CLEARLY--

149
00:06:18,847 --> 00:06:21,482
YES, DEAR.
YES, DEAR.

150
00:06:21,515 --> 00:06:22,950
I'M DOING IT, DEAR.

151
00:06:22,983 --> 00:06:24,252
YES, DEAR.

152
00:06:24,285 --> 00:06:25,487
WHO WAS IT THAT SAID,
"I NEVER MET A KID I LIKED?"

153
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,222
W.C. FIELDS, I THINK.
WELL, THAT'S THE WAY

154
00:06:27,255 --> 00:06:28,388
I FEEL ABOUT 'EM
WHEN THEY'RE ON MY BOAT.

155
00:06:28,422 --> 00:06:32,727
OH, I MEAN US.

156
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:35,162
2,000 FLUSHES, THE MOVIE.

157
00:06:40,535 --> 00:06:44,305
SOMETHING VAGUE
THIS WAY COMES.

158
00:06:44,338 --> 00:06:45,773
CARL, ARE YOU
LISTENING TO ME?

159
00:06:45,807 --> 00:06:47,408
YEAH, MOLLY,
I'M LISTENING TO YOU.

160
00:06:47,442 --> 00:06:51,978
MOSTLY, I'M EATING.

161
00:06:52,012 --> 00:06:53,480
YOU KNOW WHAT SHE HAD
THE NERVE TO SAY?

162
00:06:53,513 --> 00:06:54,548
YOU KNOW WHAT SHE SAID?

163
00:06:54,582 --> 00:06:57,218
WHAT SHE SAID, AFTER THIS.

164
00:06:57,252 --> 00:06:58,352
OW!

165
00:06:58,385 --> 00:07:00,020
OH, CARL,
DID YOU CUT YOURSELF?

166
00:07:00,053 --> 00:07:01,522
RELAX, I MEAN,
IT'S JUST A SCRATCH.

167
00:07:01,555 --> 00:07:04,358
AND IT COULD GET INFECTED.
I'LL GO GET THE IODINE.

168
00:07:04,392 --> 00:07:09,563
OOH. IT'S GERTRUDE STEIN.

169
00:07:09,597 --> 00:07:10,965
[GROWLING]

170
00:07:10,998 --> 00:07:16,570
WELL, I CAN EAT THE BOAT,
AND SPIT THEM OUT, I SUPPOSE.

171
00:07:16,603 --> 00:07:19,407
WE NOW RETURN
TO THE CUT FINGER STORY.

172
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:27,648
MAN, IT'S FARTHER UP
THAN I THOUGHT.

173
00:07:27,682 --> 00:07:29,417
THIS IS TAKING FOREVER.

174
00:07:34,855 --> 00:07:38,558
AAH, SAVE THE METAMUCIL.

175
00:07:38,592 --> 00:07:42,730
FILM CREW'S REALLY HAVING FUN
THROWING STUFF AT HER.

176
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:45,700
- CARL! CARL!
- CAW! CAW!

177
00:07:45,733 --> 00:07:48,402
[CARL SCREAMING]

178
00:07:48,435 --> 00:07:50,605
I GUESS HE DIDN'T LIKE
THE PORK TARTARE.

179
00:07:57,778 --> 00:08:00,347
- CARL?
- MRS. KILROY WAS HERE.

180
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:02,350
CARLY?

181
00:08:02,383 --> 00:08:05,452
LET ME CLEAR THE TABLE OFF
FOR YOU MA'AM. THANKS.

182
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,488
OUR SPECIAL TONIGHT
IS DEVIL FISH

183
00:08:07,522 --> 00:08:13,493
WITH SATANIC STRING BEANS
AND DEEP-LUCIFERED POTATOES.

184
00:08:13,527 --> 00:08:19,900
- [SCREAMING]
- THIS FISH HAS A LOT OF NERVE.

185
00:08:19,933 --> 00:08:21,902
OOH, YEAH, WE GOT DOLPHINS
IN THE BASEMENT.

186
00:08:21,935 --> 00:08:25,372
UH-OH.

187
00:08:25,405 --> 00:08:28,508
NO! WRONG! DO IT AGAIN.

188
00:08:28,542 --> 00:08:31,478
[DOLPHINS CLICKING]

189
00:08:31,512 --> 00:08:37,485
♪ THIS IS THE DAWNING
OF THE AGE OF SEAQUARIUM ♪

190
00:08:37,518 --> 00:08:40,588
PETER FRAMPTON!

191
00:08:40,622 --> 00:08:42,990
[LAUGHING]

192
00:08:43,023 --> 00:08:46,360
MAN, THE STATEN ISLAND FERRY
IS WAY OFF COURSE.

193
00:08:46,393 --> 00:08:49,797
♪♪ [HUMMING]

194
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:52,800
NO, DON'T PUT ME IN THERE!
THERE'S SHARKS IN THERE!

195
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:54,402
OH, WAIT.

196
00:08:59,907 --> 00:09:02,677
HEY, TEMP-WORKERS.

197
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:05,545
I'M PLEASED AT THINGS.

198
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,548
NO, NO, I'M NOT
GONNA FALL FOR THAT.

199
00:09:07,582 --> 00:09:10,685
NO, REALLY, I AM
GETTING DIVORCED, TOOTS.

200
00:09:10,685 --> 00:09:13,087
OH, YOU.

201
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,090
HEY, FISH NOW!

202
00:09:17,123 --> 00:09:18,792
HEY, YOU HAVEN'T THANKED ME.

203
00:09:18,825 --> 00:09:20,662
COME HERE, DONALD.
COME ON.

204
00:09:20,695 --> 00:09:25,600
HEY, DON'T CALL ME DONALD.
MY NAME IS... [DOLPHIN SOUNDS]

205
00:09:25,633 --> 00:09:28,202
AH.

206
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:29,570
SHUSH UP.

207
00:09:29,603 --> 00:09:31,605
NOW, HOW WOULD YOU
RATE THAT FISH?

208
00:09:31,672 --> 00:09:33,007
YOU'VE HAD ENOUGH.

209
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:36,210
[CHOKING]
UGH, WHAT DID YOU PUT
IN THAT FISH?

210
00:09:36,243 --> 00:09:39,180
YOU'RE A FATTY!

211
00:09:39,213 --> 00:09:42,048
NOW THAT CONCLUDES
OUR TOUR INSIDE.

212
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:45,252
OUTSIDE, THE OUTDOOR POOL,
WHERE THE DOLPHINS ARE TOGETHER

213
00:09:45,285 --> 00:09:47,522
WITH RESEARCHER STELLA DICKENS,
THEIR TRAINER.

214
00:09:47,555 --> 00:09:50,523
THIS WAY.

215
00:09:50,557 --> 00:09:51,958
- ISN'T THAT SOMETHING?
- THEY CAN MOVE.

216
00:09:51,992 --> 00:09:53,193
WHAT DO YOU DO EXACTLY?

217
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:56,130
I STUDY THEIR BEHAVIOR
HERE IN CAPTIVITY,

218
00:09:56,163 --> 00:09:58,532
AND ALSO
IN THEIR NATURAL HABITAT.

219
00:09:58,565 --> 00:10:01,135
AND RIGHT NOW, DR. BOB HOGAN,
MY ASSOCIATE,

220
00:10:01,168 --> 00:10:03,270
IS AT SEA,
CONDUCTING AN EXPERIMENT.

221
00:10:03,303 --> 00:10:09,510
DR. BOB HOGAN'S ALSO
EXPERIMENTING WITH FILM CREDITS.

222
00:10:09,543 --> 00:10:14,848
DEVIL FISH, THE STORY
OF ALEISTER CRAPPIE.

223
00:10:14,848 --> 00:10:19,220
HEY LOOK, THEY SPELLED
HIS NAME SIDEWAYS.

224
00:10:19,253 --> 00:10:23,123
IT'S A MAN WEARING
A LONDON PHONE BOOTH.

225
00:10:23,157 --> 00:10:24,592
HEY, A TURTLE.

226
00:10:24,625 --> 00:10:27,293
SO, MIKE, TURTLES EXCRETE WAX,
AND YOU HUMANS PUT IT IN CANS

227
00:10:27,328 --> 00:10:28,895
AND JUST RUB IT
ALL OVER YOUR CARS?

228
00:10:28,928 --> 00:10:32,098
GOOD, THAT'S GOOD.
JUST KEEP DOING THAT.

229
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:34,602
THAT'S NOT EXACTLY
HOW IT GOES.

230
00:10:37,905 --> 00:10:44,578
SAY, UH, WHOSE FISH IS THIS?
SOMEBODY LOSE THIS FISH?

231
00:10:44,612 --> 00:10:48,682
MAN, FEEDING
THE WHOLE OCEAN IS HARD.

232
00:10:48,715 --> 00:10:53,753
♪ DON'T SAY THINGS
YOU'RE GONNA... ♪

233
00:10:53,787 --> 00:10:55,655
GENERAL ORGANIZER,
JUST PUT SOME THINGS

234
00:10:55,690 --> 00:11:02,028
OVER THERE AND OVER THERE.

235
00:11:02,062 --> 00:11:03,863
THEY'RE GOING TO AIR-LIFT US
OUT OF THE MOVIE!

236
00:11:03,897 --> 00:11:06,800
- HERE WE ARE! HERE WE ARE!
- RIGHT HERE! HERE!

237
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,668
- AH.
- HEY!

238
00:11:08,702 --> 00:11:11,705
[BOOM]

239
00:11:11,738 --> 00:11:12,707
- AH.
- DOESN'T SEE US.

240
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:14,642
1-4-2-1 HERE. 1-4-2-1.

241
00:11:14,675 --> 00:11:16,877
WE'RE OVER THE AREA.
NO SIGN OF ANYTHING YET.

242
00:11:16,910 --> 00:11:18,312
WHILE THERE ARE THINGS,
OF COURSE,

243
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:21,815
I ENGAGE IN HYPERBOLE
TO MAKE A POINT, HOWEVER.

244
00:11:21,848 --> 00:11:25,618
AH, WHAT A GREAT JOB. I'M GLAD
I WUSSED OUT OF VIETNAM.

245
00:11:31,325 --> 00:11:35,062
MAN, WHAT A CRUMMY
BOAT DESIGN.

246
00:11:35,095 --> 00:11:37,832
- OKAY, 1-4-2-1 HERE.
- YEAH.

247
00:11:37,865 --> 00:11:39,933
WE SPOTTED HIM.

248
00:11:39,967 --> 00:11:44,037
WE WILL ATTEMPT RECOUP.

249
00:11:44,072 --> 00:11:47,842
♪ DEVIL FISH IN LOVE ♪

250
00:11:47,875 --> 00:11:52,813
♪ DEVIL FISH IN LOVE ♪

251
00:11:56,283 --> 00:11:58,785
DONALD.

252
00:11:58,818 --> 00:12:00,587
WELL, HOW DO YOU DO, SIR?

253
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:02,657
YEAH, YEAH, BANTER,
BANTER, BANTER, FISH!

254
00:12:02,690 --> 00:12:07,060
NICE TO KNOW YOU.
VERY GOOD.

255
00:12:07,093 --> 00:12:08,462
THERE YOU GO.

256
00:12:08,495 --> 00:12:10,932
WHEN DUMB GUYS SNORKEL.

257
00:12:10,965 --> 00:12:12,500
- READY, MAN?
- RIGHT!

258
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:13,700
GO!

259
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:16,370
- AAH!
- OH, GREAT COAST GUARD.

260
00:12:16,403 --> 00:12:20,307
IT'S GONNA BE COLD!

261
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:26,247
PLEASE.

262
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,848
GET THE HARNESS OUT.

263
00:12:27,882 --> 00:12:32,887
- GET THE HARDNESS OUT?
- THAT'S WHAT I HEARD.

264
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:39,193
HANG ON, OLD CHUM.
HA, I KID THE DEAD GUY.

265
00:12:39,227 --> 00:12:40,193
- [LAUGHTER]
- WOW.

266
00:12:40,227 --> 00:12:43,230
I'M GETTING DIZZY.

267
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:48,202
OH, ISN'T THIS AN ORANGE JUICE?
OH, DARN.

268
00:12:48,235 --> 00:12:51,172
THE DIRECTOR'S VISION,
LOTS OF SHOTS OF THINGS.

269
00:12:51,205 --> 00:12:53,207
STAND BY TO HARNESS.

270
00:12:57,978 --> 00:13:04,452
♪ TOO MUCH TIME
ON MY HANDS ♪

271
00:13:04,485 --> 00:13:06,953
UH, IS THIS GUY THAT IMPORTANT?
WHY DON'T THEY JUST LEAVE HIM?

272
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:10,892
I DON'T KNOW.

273
00:13:10,925 --> 00:13:12,827
EARLY PARASAILING.

274
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:16,097
GIVE STELLA A BIG HUG.
COME ON. UP, UP, UP...

275
00:13:16,130 --> 00:13:18,465
[APPLAUSE]

276
00:13:18,498 --> 00:13:20,067
YOU KNOW,
JUST BECAUSE YOU CAN EDIT,

277
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:22,068
DOESN'T MEAN YOU SHOULD.

278
00:13:22,102 --> 00:13:24,838
I TRIED TO UNCLOG MY LAWNMOWER
WITH MY FEET.

279
00:13:24,872 --> 00:13:31,045
OOH.

280
00:13:31,078 --> 00:13:34,182
COME ON, BEER,
GET IN MY MOUTH. COME ON!

281
00:13:34,215 --> 00:13:36,850
[INSTRUMENTS WHIRRING]

282
00:13:36,883 --> 00:13:37,918
[IMITATING NOISES]

283
00:13:37,952 --> 00:13:39,920
I'VE LOCATED
A GARY WRIGHT SONG.

284
00:13:48,395 --> 00:13:49,863
MY GOODNESS.
THAT'S MY SPECIAL LINE.

285
00:13:49,897 --> 00:13:55,235
A BEER
IS IN TROUBLE SOMEWHERE.

286
00:13:55,268 --> 00:13:59,973
AH, TRANSPORT ME, MARC COHN.

287
00:14:00,007 --> 00:14:03,210
I FEEL LIKE I ACTUALLY AM
WALKING IN MEMPHIS.

288
00:14:08,115 --> 00:14:11,518
HUH, I DIDN'T KNOW HUMANS
COULD SURVIVE WITHOUT FLESH.

289
00:14:15,088 --> 00:14:16,923
DONALD, MINNIE, WHAT'S WRONG?

290
00:14:16,957 --> 00:14:19,893
- [RACECAR SOUNDS]
- WHAT'S WRONG?

291
00:14:19,927 --> 00:14:22,897
DONALD!

292
00:14:22,930 --> 00:14:25,132
WHAT IS IT?

293
00:14:25,165 --> 00:14:29,937
I BET THEY HAVE BEAUTIFUL
HARDWOOD UNDER THAT CARPETING.

294
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:31,972
MINNIE, STOP! STOP IT!

295
00:14:32,005 --> 00:14:33,107
WHAT'S WRONG?

296
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:39,680
♪♪

297
00:14:39,713 --> 00:14:41,648
I'M OUT OF BEER.

298
00:14:41,682 --> 00:14:43,950
IT'S COMING
RIGHT AT THE BOAT!

299
00:14:43,983 --> 00:14:46,453
OH, MY GOD.

300
00:14:46,487 --> 00:14:49,757
THEY HANGED BOBO!

301
00:14:49,790 --> 00:14:53,293
COME ON, LEGS, EVOLVE!

302
00:14:53,327 --> 00:14:54,928
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

303
00:14:54,962 --> 00:14:56,263
WHAT'S HAPPENED?

304
00:14:56,297 --> 00:14:59,933
- MINNIE! DONALD!
- CLARENCE! PAUL! RAIF! LUIGI!

305
00:14:59,967 --> 00:15:04,838
[SCREAMING]

306
00:15:04,872 --> 00:15:09,477
WELL, SHE'S TOO GRISTLY,
TOO MUCH BONE TO EAT.

307
00:15:09,510 --> 00:15:12,012
SAY, WE'RE ABOUT TO HAVE
ONE OF OUR DOLPHIN ORGIES,

308
00:15:12,045 --> 00:15:13,647
IF YOU'RE...

309
00:15:20,387 --> 00:15:21,388
[YELPS]

310
00:15:21,422 --> 00:15:23,490
AH, THEY PANTSED ME.

311
00:15:28,562 --> 00:15:34,468
HIS HAIR'S GETTING ALL TANGLED
IN THE REEL-TO-REEL.

312
00:15:34,502 --> 00:15:40,473
HE'S LISTENING TO "AWAKEN
THE BEER DRINKER WITHIN."

313
00:15:40,507 --> 00:15:46,813
I DID MY OWN SPLENECTOMY
AND SAVED.

314
00:15:46,847 --> 00:15:48,948
WELL, DOC,
WHAT'S THE STORY?

315
00:15:48,982 --> 00:15:50,950
RUNAWAY BUNNY.

316
00:15:50,985 --> 00:15:53,387
AT FIRST SIGHT,
I'D SAY IT WAS A SHARK.

317
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:54,722
AND A BIG ONE AT THAT.

318
00:15:54,755 --> 00:15:56,657
BUT NOT NECESSARILY.

319
00:15:56,690 --> 00:15:58,092
LOOK.

320
00:15:58,125 --> 00:15:59,627
WHOA! ONE THING'S
NOT BIT OFF.

321
00:15:59,693 --> 00:16:01,295
THE BITE IS CLEAN
LIKE A SHARK'S,

322
00:16:01,328 --> 00:16:03,463
BUT THE TEETH MARKS
PUZZLED ME.

323
00:16:03,497 --> 00:16:05,532
AND SO DOES
THE SIZE OF THE BITE.

324
00:16:05,565 --> 00:16:07,668
FOR ME IT COULD HAVE BEEN CAUSED
BY SOMETHING ELSE.

325
00:16:07,702 --> 00:16:08,835
OTHER THAN A SHARK, THAT IS.

326
00:16:08,868 --> 00:16:10,103
I DID IT.

327
00:16:10,137 --> 00:16:11,638
WELL, YOU COULD HAVE
THE BODY PHOTOGRAPHED.

328
00:16:11,672 --> 00:16:13,073
WOULDN'T HURT.

329
00:16:13,107 --> 00:16:14,608
- TAKE CARE OF IT, CORTEZ.
- DUH.

330
00:16:14,642 --> 00:16:16,643
- AND TAKE SOME SHOTS
FOR OUR RECORDS, TOO.
- DUH, OKAY.

331
00:16:16,677 --> 00:16:18,845
- OKAY, SHERIFF.
- LET'S HOPE YOU'RE WRONG.

332
00:16:18,878 --> 00:16:20,780
I USUALLY AM, SO...

333
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:23,750
I JUST DON'T UNDERSTAND
WHAT HAPPENED TO THOSE DOLPHINS.

334
00:16:23,783 --> 00:16:24,952
THEY TOOK MY CONDITIONER.

335
00:16:24,985 --> 00:16:26,887
THEY'VE NEVER
BEHAVED THIS WAY BEFORE.

336
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,623
- QUIET A SECOND, STELLA.
- HEY, THEY ALMOST
KILLED ME, BOB!

337
00:16:29,657 --> 00:16:31,125
ARE YOU LISTENING TO ME?

338
00:16:31,158 --> 00:16:34,428
I'D SAY SOMETHING EXTRAORDINARY
HAPPENED TO BOTH OF US, THEN.

339
00:16:34,462 --> 00:16:36,763
I MADE A RECORDING.
TELL ME WHAT YOU THINK.

340
00:16:36,797 --> 00:16:39,032
WHATEVER IT WAS,
IT ALMOST MADE ME CAPSIZE.

341
00:16:39,065 --> 00:16:40,733
[GULPING]

342
00:16:40,767 --> 00:16:42,102
[LIP SMACKING, CANS OPENING]

343
00:16:42,135 --> 00:16:45,005
[DRINKING SOUNDS CONTINUE]

344
00:16:50,643 --> 00:16:52,045
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

345
00:16:52,078 --> 00:16:54,147
I'M SURE I RECORDED IT.

346
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,715
RECORDED WHAT?

347
00:16:55,748 --> 00:16:59,520
THAT SOUND.
THAT STRANGE SOUND.

348
00:16:59,553 --> 00:17:01,588
I'VE NEVER HEARD
ANYTHING LIKE IT.

349
00:17:01,622 --> 00:17:04,592
- IT WAS ALMOST LIKE A VOICE.
- A VOICE?

350
00:17:04,658 --> 00:17:06,593
DID I SAY VOICE?
I MEANT DOORKNOB.

351
00:17:06,627 --> 00:17:09,530
NO, NOT EXACTLY
A VOICE, IT...

352
00:17:09,563 --> 00:17:12,198
WAS MORE OF
A TERRIFYING SOUND.

353
00:17:12,232 --> 00:17:14,033
- FULL OF HATE.
- HATE?

354
00:17:14,067 --> 00:17:16,170
YEAH, YEAH, THAT'S IT.

355
00:17:16,203 --> 00:17:17,872
- HATE.
- OH, BOB DORNAN.

356
00:17:17,905 --> 00:17:20,073
WHEN DID YOU HEAR IT?

357
00:17:20,107 --> 00:17:22,208
AT ABOUT 10:00.

358
00:17:22,242 --> 00:17:24,578
WAIT, I'LL CHECK MY NOTES.

359
00:17:24,612 --> 00:17:27,713
YES, HERE IT IS. 10:00,
HEARD VOICE FILLED WITH HATE.

360
00:17:27,748 --> 00:17:29,650
I PICKED IT UP AT 10:18.

361
00:17:29,683 --> 00:17:31,418
AND IT LASTED
FOR THREE MINUTES.

362
00:17:31,452 --> 00:17:32,618
LIKE MY LAST 12-PACK.

363
00:17:32,652 --> 00:17:33,887
THAT'S EXACTLY
THE TIME THE DOLPHINS

364
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:36,690
STARTED GOING IN CIRCLES.

365
00:17:36,723 --> 00:17:39,693
DON'T YOU THINK
THERE'S A CONNECTION THERE?

366
00:17:39,727 --> 00:17:41,495
WHY DIDN'T I GET IT ON TAPE?

367
00:17:41,528 --> 00:17:42,695
BECAUSE YOU WERE DRUNK?

368
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:45,065
MAYBE IT WAS TOO HIGH
OR TOO LOW A FREQUENCY.

369
00:17:45,098 --> 00:17:47,133
KENNETH.

370
00:17:47,167 --> 00:17:49,202
THEN YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M THINKING?

371
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:51,538
THAT PETER IS THE ONLY ONE
THAT CAN HELP US.

372
00:17:51,572 --> 00:17:52,705
YEAH, PETER ALLEN.

373
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:56,210
- PETER?
- ALLEN.

374
00:17:56,243 --> 00:17:59,312
MAN, ABYSS II
ISN'T VERY GOOD.

375
00:17:59,345 --> 00:18:01,882
♪♪

376
00:18:01,915 --> 00:18:03,750
IS THAT FAB OR ROB?

377
00:18:10,257 --> 00:18:13,060
UGH, YOU COLORED GIRLS
WHO HAVE CONSIDERED SUICIDE

378
00:18:13,093 --> 00:18:18,598
WHEN THE RAINBOW IS ENUF.
[CHUCKLES]

379
00:18:18,632 --> 00:18:21,568
- YOU CALL THIS WORKING?
- WHAT?

380
00:18:21,602 --> 00:18:23,670
I SAID,
"DO YOU CALL THIS WORKING?"

381
00:18:23,703 --> 00:18:26,307
- I CAN'T HEAR YOU.
- I'M LISTENING TO SHONEN KNIFE.

382
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:28,342
♪♪ [MUSIC STOPS]
NOW YOU CAN HEAR ME.

383
00:18:28,375 --> 00:18:30,043
YOU THINK?

384
00:18:30,077 --> 00:18:32,245
WELL, HOW ABOUT THAT MONITOR
THAT NEEDED FIXING?

385
00:18:32,278 --> 00:18:34,615
I CHECKED ALL THE CIRCUITS,
AND THEY'RE ALL SCREWED UP.

386
00:18:34,648 --> 00:18:36,317
- IMPOSSIBLE TO FIX.
- AW.

387
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:38,885
THE ONLY THING THAT'S SCREWED UP
IS YOUR HEAD.

388
00:18:38,918 --> 00:18:40,687
THE ONLY THING THAT'S SCREWED UP
IS YOUR HEAD.

389
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:43,157
- WHAT THE--?
- WHAT WAS THAT?

390
00:18:43,190 --> 00:18:45,192
THE ONLY THING
THAT'S SCREWED UP, FUNNY MAN,

391
00:18:45,225 --> 00:18:47,727
- IS YOUR HEAD.
- HELLO?

392
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:50,330
MM, THAT'S BECAUSE
YOU'RE A GENIUS.

393
00:18:50,363 --> 00:18:53,800
LOOK, IT TOOK ME FIVE YEARS
TO MAKE THIS PLACE GO.

394
00:18:53,833 --> 00:18:55,768
TRY NOT TO DESTROY IT
IN THE NEXT TEN DAYS.

395
00:18:55,802 --> 00:18:57,270
WHEN ARE YOU LEAVING?

396
00:18:57,303 --> 00:18:59,640
RIGHT NOW, SANDRA.

397
00:18:59,673 --> 00:19:01,708
AND IF THERE'S
ANYTHING ELSE YOU NEED...

398
00:19:01,742 --> 00:19:03,177
WHY DON'T YOU
TAKE ME WITH YOU?

399
00:19:03,210 --> 00:19:04,812
BECAUSE YOUR DRESS
LIKE ROBIN WILLIAMS.

400
00:19:04,845 --> 00:19:06,913
BECAUSE SOMEBODY
HAS TO WATCH THE STORE.

401
00:19:06,947 --> 00:19:08,715
BECAUSE THERE'S ABOUT
THREE GORGEOUS LADIES

402
00:19:08,748 --> 00:19:09,817
WAITING FOR ME IN NEW YORK.

403
00:19:09,850 --> 00:19:11,885
THE DELRUBIO SISTERS.

404
00:19:11,918 --> 00:19:14,020
HEADS UP, SANDRA.

405
00:19:14,053 --> 00:19:18,392
RIBBIT.

406
00:19:18,425 --> 00:19:20,193
OF COURSE I AM AMERICAN
AND NOT ITALIAN.

407
00:19:20,227 --> 00:19:24,832
I DRIVE A TRUCK.

408
00:19:24,865 --> 00:19:26,833
♪♪ [HUMMING]

409
00:19:26,867 --> 00:19:28,735
I THINK I'LL PUT UP THE SAIL.

410
00:19:33,907 --> 00:19:35,942
- HI, PETER.
- HI, STICK.

411
00:19:35,942 --> 00:19:38,145
- HI, STELLA.
- I NEED YOUR HELP.

412
00:19:38,178 --> 00:19:40,113
OH, NO, I'M GOING
ON VACATION.

413
00:19:40,147 --> 00:19:42,917
ONLY GOT A COUPLE OF SECONDS
TO SPARE.

414
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:45,452
A GENIUS
DOESN'T NEED ANY MORE.

415
00:19:45,485 --> 00:19:46,987
WHAT'S THIS?

416
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:48,888
I'M THINKING OF BECOMING
DARYL HANNAH.

417
00:19:48,922 --> 00:19:52,192
IT'S A LIST OF THE EQUIPMENT
THAT BOB AND I'LL NEED.

418
00:19:52,225 --> 00:19:53,560
YOU'VE GOT TO BE KIDDING.

419
00:19:53,593 --> 00:19:55,162
I'D HAVE TO GO TO AMERICA--
OH, WAIT.

420
00:19:55,195 --> 00:19:58,398
I'M GOING AWAY. THIS STUFF'S
ALL GOTTA BE BUILT TO SPECS.

421
00:19:58,432 --> 00:20:00,000
- PLEASE.
- I'M SKINNY.

422
00:20:00,033 --> 00:20:02,368
IT'S VERY IMPORTANT.

423
00:20:02,402 --> 00:20:04,303
WHO ELSE CAN I TURN TO?

424
00:20:04,337 --> 00:20:07,807
UGH, TAKE AT LEAST A DAY.

425
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:10,177
YEAH, AND YOU CAN DO IT
IN A FEW HOURS.

426
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:11,812
HMM?

427
00:20:11,845 --> 00:20:14,380
I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

428
00:20:14,413 --> 00:20:16,750
ENJOY THE SIDES
OF MY BREASTS.

429
00:20:16,783 --> 00:20:19,018
SURE-- OH.

430
00:20:19,052 --> 00:20:23,890
WHO WAS THAT, AND HOW
DO WE KNOW EACH OTHER?

431
00:20:23,923 --> 00:20:29,630
TINY MEDICAL CENTER,
STARRING TINY CHAD EVERETT.

432
00:20:29,663 --> 00:20:34,233
HEY, THAT'S RIP TORN IN DRAG.

433
00:20:34,267 --> 00:20:38,938
WELCOME TO THE WORLD
OF "WOI."

434
00:20:38,972 --> 00:20:44,410
YES, HERE AT WOI,
WE DO THIS KIND OF THING.

435
00:20:44,443 --> 00:20:48,982
[IMITATING DRUMS
AND ANIMALS CHATTERING]

436
00:20:49,015 --> 00:20:53,987
GOTTA FINISH THIS BOMB
FOR PAKISTAN BY SATURDAY.

437
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:57,557
SOMEBODY SWIPED
THE MICROWAVE.

438
00:20:57,590 --> 00:21:00,027
I AM PERFECTING THE FIZZY.

439
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:02,328
YES.

440
00:21:04,463 --> 00:21:09,102
[COMPUTERIZED VOICE]
I LOVE YOU, DAVIS.

441
00:21:09,135 --> 00:21:12,438
[IMITATING VOICE]
HI, HONEY. I'M HERE.

442
00:21:12,472 --> 00:21:14,507
WHO ELSE
WOULD IT HAVE BEEN?

443
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:16,310
NOT LARRY STORCH,
I DON'T THINK.

444
00:21:16,343 --> 00:21:18,245
BUT YOU SHOULD BE MORE CAREFUL.

445
00:21:18,278 --> 00:21:19,545
WHY?

446
00:21:19,578 --> 00:21:21,548
SOMEONE MIGHT
INTERCEPT THE MESSAGE.

447
00:21:21,582 --> 00:21:23,350
HMM.
IT'S NOT LIKELY, THOUGH.

448
00:21:23,383 --> 00:21:25,852
MY HUSBAND'S ONLY INTERESTED
IN WINNING A NOBEL,

449
00:21:25,885 --> 00:21:28,688
AND THE OTHERS ARE MUCH TOO BUSY
TO WORRY ABOUT US.

450
00:21:28,722 --> 00:21:30,223
WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN?

451
00:21:30,257 --> 00:21:32,325
ON THE CHALLENGER, WE TOOK
SOME SAMPLES OF PLANKTON.

452
00:21:32,358 --> 00:21:34,160
THE SEA WAS MARVELOUS.

453
00:21:34,193 --> 00:21:36,997
I HEARD THEY FISHED ANOTHER
DEAD BODY FROM THE OCEAN.

454
00:21:37,030 --> 00:21:38,465
GOT HIM IN THE NETS.

455
00:21:38,498 --> 00:21:41,167
OH, I'LL BET THEY'LL
COME AROUND BOTHERING US AGAIN.

456
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:42,435
